# ReadMe

The programmed is coded in and needs to be ran in a C++ environment.
If g++ is installed run the following to compile:
    g++ montyHall.cpp - o monty
Once compiled run the following to run the program:
    ./monty
The simulate option always chooses to switch. I intend to change that for user to decided but it is how it is.
I didn't quite understand how to exactly switching answers gave you a better chance and to be honest I still don't really. Was surprised to see how much of an advantage it gives the person.
